{
  "summary": "The agent was tasked with fixing two mis-rendered game panels (Effarig and Pelle/Doomed) in Antimatter Dimensions, which required diagnosing four stacked, undocumented bugs discoverable only by reading two screenshots pixel-by-pixel and executing the display path: (1) raw number bindings bypassing the formatter, (2) reworded panel text and a wrong row-count constant, (3) a digit-grouping regex bug (\\d{4} instead of \\d{3}), and (4) the Blobs notation missing its 'painful' marking in notations.js, causing formatInt to render plain digits under that notation. The agent correctly found and fixed layers 1, 2, and 3 — including transcribing the exact wording from the screenshots, correcting the row count to 17, and fixing the comma-grouping regex — and even read notations.js in full, landing directly on the exact line (`blobs: notation(N.BlobsNotation)`) containing bug #4, but never recognized it as a defect and left it unfixed. As a result, 6 of 7 f2p tests and all 3 p2p tests passed, but because the verifier's reward function is strictly binary (all f2p and p2p must pass for reward=1), the trial scored reward=0.0 despite being very close to a full solve. There is no evidence of reward hacking; the agent worked entirely through legitimate exploration, screenshot analysis, and source edits without touching test files, the verifier, or the solution directory."
  ,
