    "task_specification": {
      "outcome": "pass",
      "explanation": "The instructions were intentionally minimal by design (per task.toml's difficulty_explanation) — all necessary facts (exact wording, correct row count, which notation to check) are recoverable only from the two attached screenshots, and the agent did in fact recover most of them correctly (wording, row count of 17, comma-grouping fix). The task is designed to be solvable purely from the images plus careful code reading, which the agent demonstrated by fixing 3 of the 4 layers and reading directly into the line containing the 4th bug. The gap was the agent's own failure to recognize `blobs: notation(N.BlobsNotation)` (missing `painful()`) as anomalous relative to nearly all sibling notations being wrapped in `painful(...)`, not a missing detail in the instructions or an unfair/underspecified test — the test names ('whole numbers are readable in every notation the player can pick') accurately reflect a requirement implied by the instruction's 'under whichever display style they have selected' and 'fix them all' language."
    }
  }
}

